          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.078,
            0.744,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": "There are many materials through which you are not able to see at all. These materials are called **opaque**. Wood, cardboard and metals are examples of opaque materials."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.139,
            0.744,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "The materials through which objects can be seen, but not clearly, are known as **translucent**. Butter paper and frosted glass are examples of translucent materials."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.199,
            0.744,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "Look at Fig. 6.5. Identify and label the nature of materials used by Ghulan (A), Sheeta (B), Sara (C) and Sheeta’s brother (D)."
